---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import ProjectLayout from '../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

import ourwall1 from '../../assets/images/projects/ourwall/ourwall1.png';
import ourwall2 from '../../assets/images/projects/ourwall/ourwall2.png';
import ourwall3 from '../../assets/images/projects/ourwall/ourwall3.png';
import ourwall4 from '../../assets/images/projects/ourwall/ourwall4.png';
import ourwall5 from '../../assets/images/projects/ourwall/ourwall5.png';
import ourwall6 from '../../assets/images/projects/ourwall/ourwall6.png';
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Our Wall - Artem Androsov"
  description="Our Wall — an anonymous social network designed around one premise: remove identity and people say what they actually think."
  ogImage="/og/ourwall.jpg"
  activePage="projects"
>
        <div class="back-nav">
            <a href="/" class="back-link">Back to projects</a>
        </div>

        <section class="project-hero" id="hero">
            <div class="section-label">Case study</div>
            <h1>Our Wall</h1>
            <p class="project-brief">An anonymous social network built on one premise: people perform online because
                they're afraid. Remove identity — and the wall shows what people actually think. Designed the product
                logic, built v1 with AI-assisted code in one week, survived a public attack on launch day, and shipped
                v2 with a developer who broke in and then offered to rebuild it properly.</p>

            <div class="project-meta">
                <div class="meta-item">
                    <span class="meta-label">My role</span>
                    <span class="meta-value">Product, UX</span>
                </div>
                <div class="meta-item">
                    <span class="meta-label">Areas</span>
                    <div class="meta-tags">
                        <span class="meta-tag">Product Strategy</span>
                        <span class="meta-tag">UX Design</span>
                        <span class="meta-tag">Community Design</span>
                        <span class="meta-tag">Self-initiated</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="project-concept" id="concept">
            <div class="www-grid">
                <div class="www-column">
                    <h2 class="www-title">Why</h2>
                    <p class="www-text">Social networks optimise for performance. People post what gets engagement, not
                        what they actually think — a curated version of themselves. The gap between what people feel and
                        what they say online is enormous, and it's not a Russian problem or a political problem: it's a
                        human one. Threads fills with fake income screenshots. Instagram with highlight reels. Twitter
                        with takes performed for an audience. I wanted to build the opposite: a space with no profiles,
                        no followers, no reputation to protect. Just thoughts, appearing and disappearing — like chalk
                        on a wall. The anonymity isn't a feature. It's the entire product premise.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="www-column">
                    <h2 class="www-title">What</h2>
                    <p class="www-text">I designed the full product logic before writing a single line of code: the
                        ephemeral timeline, the mood system, the reaction mechanics, the community moderation threshold.
                        The mood system lets you tag each thought with an emotional state — each mood has an emoji, a
                        colour, and a colour-coded card on the wall. Reactions work like Telegram — a set of emojis, no
                        like counts. Moderation is crowdsourced: five reports removes a post automatically, no admin
                        required. The FOMO mechanic was deliberate: posts disappear after a set window, creating urgency
                        to read now rather than scroll later. I iterated on the window length — starting at midnight
                        deletion, moving to 24-hour personal timers per post, then extending to one week as organic
                        traffic stabilised. Each change was a product decision, not a technical one.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="www-column">
                    <h2 class="www-title">How</h2>
                    <p class="www-text">Product logic came first — I mapped every mechanic before opening a code
                        editor. Then built v1 in one week using AI-assisted development: described the product to the
                        model, iterated on the output, adjusted visual and logic, deployed to server. The process was
                        the subject of a YouTube video showing that a working social network MVP could be built without
                        prior coding knowledge. The video brought the first users — and the first attack. Within hours
                        of launch: DDoS flood, spam injection, explicit image overwrites. I took the server down. In
                        the comments of the video, one of the people who had broken in left a public message: he'd
                        found the vulnerability, and he could fix it. We talked. He rewrote the entire codebase in
                        React. Our Wall v2 launched — with an admin panel, server health monitoring, and a moderation
                        system that held. Nobody broke it again. The project attracted a developer not through a job
                        posting, but through the quality of the idea.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="project-gallery" id="gallery">
            <div class="section-label">Process &amp; outcome</div>
            <h2>What it looks like</h2>

            <div class="gallery-grid">
                <div class="gallery-item">
                    <Image src={ourwall1} alt="Our Wall — image 1" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </div>
                <div class="gallery-item">
                    <Image src={ourwall2} alt="Our Wall — image 2" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </div>
                <div class="gallery-item">
                    <Image src={ourwall3} alt="Our Wall — image 3" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </div>
                <div class="gallery-item">
                    <Image src={ourwall4} alt="Our Wall — image 4" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </div>
                <div class="gallery-item">
                    <Image src={ourwall5} alt="Our Wall — image 5" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </div>
                <div class="gallery-item">
                    <Image src={ourwall6} alt="Our Wall — image 6" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="project-results" id="results">
            <div class="section-label">Results</div>
            <h2>What we delivered</h2>

            <div class="metrics-grid">
                <div class="metric-card">
                    <span class="metric-number">1 week</span>
                    <span class="metric-label">Time to v1</span>
                    <p class="metric-description">Full social network MVP — product logic, UI, and deployment — built solo with AI-assisted code</p>
                </div>
                <div class="metric-card">
                    <span class="metric-number">v2</span>
                    <span class="metric-label">Rebuilt under pressure</span>
                    <p class="metric-description">Attacked on launch day, rebuilt in React by a developer who found the project through the YouTube video</p>
                </div>
                <div class="metric-card">
                    <span class="metric-number">3</span>
                    <span class="metric-label">Iterated mechanics</span>
                    <p class="metric-description">FOMO window evolved: midnight delete → 24h personal timer → 7-day window. Each change driven by user behaviour, not preference</p>
                </div>
                <div class="metric-card">
                    <span class="metric-number">5</span>
                    <span class="metric-label">Reports to remove</span>
                    <p class="metric-description">Crowdsourced moderation — no admin action needed. Community self-regulates at threshold</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="project-shipped" id="shipped">
            <div class="section-label">What shipped</div>
            <p class="shipped-text">Our Wall is live at ourwall.ru — organic traffic only, zero marketing budget.
                Users still post. The mood system, reactions, comments, and community reporting all work in production.
                The product direction beyond v2 is clear: location-based walls (by café, university, neighbourhood),
                mood aggregation as a real-time sentiment layer, private community walls for events and organisations.
                The infrastructure for that exists. What's missing is investment to continue development.</p>
            <a href="https://ourwall.ru" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="display: inline-block; margin-top: 12px; color: inherit; text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 500;">View live product →</a>
        </section>

        <section class="next-project" id="next">
            <div class="section-label">Next project</div>
            <a href="/projects/gabarshop" class="next-project-link">
                <span class="next-project-name">GABARSHOP</span>
                <span class="next-project-arrow">→</span>
            </a>
        </section>

        <section class="cta-section" id="cta">
            <h2>Have an idea that needs product thinking?</h2>
            <p class="contact-subtitle contact-subtitle-margin">
                Tell me about it — I'll help you find the logic inside it.
            </p>
            <a href="https://t.me/androsovart" target="_blank" class="btn-primary" rel="noopener noreferrer">Get in
                touch</a>
        </section>

        <Footer />
</ProjectLayout>
